INSERT INTO "tasks" VALUES('task_xtDjYBBg8SS5YEYp8ZFgi','Pre-commit hook that validates task-draft files against the live task contract','Teams that draft tasks in git want mistakes caught at commit time. Write a pre-commit hook (framework: pre-commit, plus a plain .git/hooks variant documented) that validates every drafts/*.task.json file against the POST /v1/tasks contract: field presence, length limits, category and output_format enums - fetched from api.basedagents.ai/openapi.json at hook install/update time and cached, so the rules track the API without a network call on every commit.

**Acceptance**

- Runs show: a clean commit passing, a commit with an over-length description blocked with a precise message, and the cached-contract refresh path.
- Works offline after first cache; says clearly when its cache is stale.
- README covers both installation styles in under ten lines each.

---
